From: OmacVM
Subject: [PATCH] MdeModulePkg/Logo: Omarchy's logo instead of TianoCore's

What: replaces the boot logo of edk2-stable202408 (MdeModulePkg/Logo/Logo.bmp,
the TianoCore logo, 193 x 58, 8-bit) with Omarchy's wordmark: 405 x 95,
24-bit, Omarchy green (#a8cd76, the colour of Omarchy's Plymouth logo) on
black. Nothing else in edk2 changes.

Why: OmacVM.app boots its VMs through this firmware; the first thing a VM
shows should be Omarchy, not TianoCore.

How it was made: boot-logo/make-logo-bmp.py from logo.svg of Omarchy
(github.com/basecamp/omarchy, commit 6520ac7d, MIT, (c) David Heinemeier
Hansson, boot-logo/LICENSE.omarchy):
  make-logo-bmp.py logo.svg MdeModulePkg/Logo/Logo.bmp 5
Each cell of the logo's 15-unit grid is a 5 x 5 pixel block, so the edges stay
sharp. ArmVirtQemu shows it centred at the firmware's 1920 x 1080.

Upstream: OmacVM only (branding), not for edk2 or QEMU.

Test: Tests/firmware/test-firmware.py boots the built firmware with an empty
disk and checks that the screen shows exactly this bitmap, centred
(build-qemu-gpu-runtime.sh runs it; on failure the build keeps QEMU's
firmware).

Applied with `git apply` (a binary patch; it checks the original logo's hash).

diff --git a/MdeModulePkg/Logo/Logo.bmp b/MdeModulePkg/Logo/Logo.bmp
index 3e85229e17595ba1f9c59e13692a4f8362ebc850..d627c3a91a639b5bbe78c38d876fe12a2ad69afb 100644
GIT binary patch
